**Test filters.** For this step these gates run only the tests their filter selects (plus any inherited expected-red tests); put the tests this step adds or changes where a filter value finds them:
- `ui-smoke`: 
- `ui-tests`: `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.MaterialsWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.SampleEditorWindowTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.ScrollExtentTests`, `OpticalConstructor.Ui.Tests.WindowLauncherTests`

**How to implement.** The Materials window exports the selected material to its file and the shown materials to a catalogue folder, and credits a licensed material (001 §B 'Export', 'Licence attribution'; 001 §G 'Exports'; the S3.3 brief: the buttons go in the Library and Materials windows, with messages and ids; a single-entry export goes through a save dialog defaulting to the catalogues folder; a category exports to a catalogue folder; .spec-md §4 'UI': every user step is a semantic message). (1) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/ConstructorUiIdOfDomain.fs`, each a one-line doc: `type LibraryExportError with member this.caption : ControlCaption` (its `describe`); `type LibraryEntryEnvelope with member this.exportedCaption (file : FileName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <name> version <n> to <file>; that version is now pinned.`; and `type CatalogueData with member this.exportedCaption (folder : FolderName) : ControlCaption` = `Exported <k> entries to the catalogue folder <folder>; their versions are now pinned.`, `k` counting its envelopes. Both windows render their export outcomes through these alone. (2) `OpticalConstructor.Ui/MaterialsWindowView.fs`. (a) The public `pickEntryExportFile (owner : Window) (startOpt : FolderName option) (envelope : LibraryEntryEnvelope) (onPicked : FileName -> unit) : unit` is the save dialog, an IO edge in `pickLibraryFolder`'s shape (step 118): `owner.StorageProvider.SaveFilePickerAsync` with `Title = "Export library entry"`, `SuggestedFileName = envelope.content.fileName.value`, `DefaultExtension` the kind's extension without its leading dot, one `FilePickerFileType` whose pattern is `*` plus that extension, `ShowOverwritePrompt = true`, and `startOpt` resolved as `pickLibraryFolder` resolves it. A confirmed file's `Path.LocalPath` is passed as a `FileName`, posted on the UI thread. (b) The public `attributionPanel (id : ConstructorUiId) (lines : EntryAttributionLine list) : IView list` answers nothing for no line, else one vertical `StackPanel` carrying `id` that holds one wrapping `TextBlock` per line (`line.text`, max width 380). (c) `MaterialsWindowModel` gains `entryExportStatus : ControlCaption option` and `entryExportError : LibraryExportError option`, both `None` when the window opens, each with a one-line doc. (d) `member this.exportableSelection : LibraryEntryEnvelope option` is, in Browse mode, the selected material's latest envelope through `context.catalogueImports.proxy.tryLatestEnvelope id.toLibraryEntryId` (step 116), and `None` in Select mode, without a selection, for a material the seam does not hold, or on a read error. (e) `MaterialsWindowMsg` gains, each documented, `ExportSelectedMaterial of FileName` (the selected material's latest version to the file chosen in the save dialog) and `ExportShownMaterials of CatalogueExportTarget` (the materials the window shows, its text filter and facets applied, to a catalogue folder; a category facet makes it that category's export). (f) `updateMaterialsWindow`. `ExportSelectedMaterial file` is inert without a selection, and otherwise calls `context.catalogueImports.exportEntry id.toLibraryEntryId file`. `ExportShownMaterials target` calls `exportEntries` over `m.filteredEntries` (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:476`), each `e.id.toLibraryEntryId`, and `target`. `Ok` sets `entryExportStatus` to the outcome's `exportedCaption` and clears `entryExportError`; `Error e` sets `entryExportError` to `Some e` and clears `entryExportStatus`. Neither arms or disarms a gate, or changes the selection or the mode. (g) The view. In the verbs row (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:971`), in Browse mode and after Categories…: while `exportableSelection` is `Some envelope`, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportButton (ControlCaption "Export…")` resolves the owner window from the press, as `TableAndElementRotationView.fs:attachDataFileButton` does, and calls `pickEntryExportFile owner context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt envelope (fun file -> dispatch (ExportSelectedMaterial file))`. While `filteredEntries` is not empty, `verbButtonOn ConstructorUiId.materialsExportShownButton (ControlCaption "Export shown to catalogue…")` calls `pickLibraryFolder owner (ControlCaption "Export to catalogue folder") context.catalogueImports.exportFolderOpt` and dispatches `ExportShownMaterials (CatalogueExportTarget.ofFolder folder)` (step 117). After step 110's import status, when either is set, a wrapping `TextBlock` carrying `materialsExportStatusText` shows `entryExportError`'s caption in `messageColor`, or else `entryExportStatus`. The view panel (`MaterialsWindowView.fs:1096`), after the description, holds `attributionPanel ConstructorUiId.materialsAttributionPanel` over `context.catalogueImports.proxy.attributionLinesOf [ shownEntry.id.toLibraryEntryId ]` (step 114), and nothing on a read error. (3) `OpticalConstructor.Controls/UiIds.fs`, the Materials window group (`UiIds.fs:525`), under one comment line citing spec 0050 S3.3: `materialsExportButton` (`"MaterialsExportButton"`), `materialsExportShownButton` (`"MaterialsExportShownButton"`), `materialsExportStatusText` (`"MaterialsExportStatusText"`) and `materialsAttributionPanel` (`"MaterialsAttributionPanel"`). (4) Tests, in `MaterialsWindowTests`. The export and attribution facts compose `stubContext` (step 110) over the in-memory double: with `let stores = CatalogueImportProxy.createInMemory ()`, the context takes `stores.materials`, `stores.categories` and `CatalogueImportContext.create stores.proxy`, the Built-in catalogue is imported through its `importFrom (CatalogueProxy.createBuiltIn ())`, and test entries are built with step 113's fixture and put through `BuiltinCatalogue.putSealedEntries`. Files go into fresh GUID folders under `Path.Combine(AppContext.BaseDirectory, "MaterialsWindowTests")`. `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`: the four ids' texts. `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`: with `userMaterialContent` `Lab glass` selected (`SelectEntry`), `ExportSelectedMaterial` of `<folder>/Lab glass.material-json` writes the file, which the context's `readEntryFile` reads back equal to the held envelope. `entryExportStatus` is `Exported Lab glass version 1 to <file>; that version is now pinned.`, and `Lab glass`, given the catalogue Langasite's complexity and saved through `stores.materials`, resolves at versions 1 and 2. `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`: `userCategoryContent` `Lab category` holds `Lab glass` and `Lab quartz` (their `categoryOpt` set to it), and `Other glass` stays in Silicon's category. With the material-category facet applied to `Lab category` (`ApplyFacetValue`), `ExportShownMaterials` of a target folder writes a catalogue holding exactly the two materials and the category, and the status counts 3 entries. `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`: with a committed text filter `Lab glass` showing two user materials of that name, `ExportShownMaterials` sets `entryExportError` to `Some (ExportCatalogueRefusedErr _)`, the status is `None`, and the target folder does not exist; a following `ExportSelectedMaterial` that succeeds clears the error. `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`: `exportableSelection` is the held envelope of the selected `Lab glass`, `None` without a selection, and `None` for a Select-mode model over the same context and selection. `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`: `materialsWindowView` mounted headless, as the class's mounting facts mount the window's view, with `licensedMaterialContent` `PTB glass` (`CC-BY-4.0`, the citation `A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`) selected, shows `materialsAttributionPanel` holding the text `PTB glass: Licence CC-BY-4.0 — cite: A. Author, Test optical constants (2026), doi:10.0000/test`. With `RII glass` (`CC0-1.0`) selected it holds `RII glass: Licence CC0-1.0` and no `cite:`, and with `Lab glass` selected no `materialsAttributionPanel` is present.

**Acceptance.** After the Materials window is wired, its Export… and Export shown to catalogue… verbs MUST export through `exportEntry` and `exportEntries`, and its view panel MUST show the selected material's attribution; ui-smoke MUST pass; ui-tests MUST pass over the selected classes, including `the export and attribution UiIds of the Materials window are the stable intent-named ids`, `ExportSelectedMaterial writes the selected material's entry file and pins its version`, `ExportShownMaterials writes the shown materials, a category facet's included, with their user category`, `a refused Materials export shows its reason and writes nothing`, `a material the library holds is exportable, in Browse mode only`, `the Materials window shows a CC-BY material's citation and a CC0 material's licence name alone`, the count rising by 6; and build, elevation and the eleven s14 invariants MUST pass.
